igh schooler, " [:a {:href "/athletes/78191"} "Milt Campbell"] ", who finished second at the Olympic Trials in his first career decathlon."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Americans swept the medals, with Campbell second and Simmons repeating his bronze medal effort. But the 1952 Olympic decathlon was simply a coronation for Mathias, who became the first man to defend the decathlon gold medal. In the process, he broke his own world record, and defeated Campbell by over 900 points."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Mathias effectively retired after Helsinki, although he returned in 1956 to win a military decathlon, ending his career undefeated in 11 competitions. Mathias was also a star football player at Stanford, competing in the Rose Bowl. He later had a brief Hollywood career, and then served three terms in the U.S. House of Representatives."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Points (1962 Tables)"] [:th {} "Points (1985 Hand Tables)"] [:th {} "Points (1985 Auto Tables)"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1039"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78742"} "Bob Mathias"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "7887"] [:td {} "7731"] [:td {} "7580"] [:td {} "7589"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1040"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78191"} "Milt Campbell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "6975"] [:td {} "7132"] [:td {} "6948"] [:td {} "6986"] [:td {}